Let each writer name its own locks

The lock code held one definition of the two lock file names. Every
binary that links it then takes the same daemon lock and the same
write lock. A second writer of another file set needs a pair of its
own. The two writers hold no file in common, so one shared write lock
costs contention and buys nothing.

The definitions move into the main file of the binary, and lock.h
keeps the extern declarations. The lock functions read the names
through those declarations, so no signature changes and the two names
of this writer stay the same.

The change sits on the branch work/firefox-theme of the local tree, as
commit 1 of 10. The branch holds those ten commits above the head of
work/gtk4-theme, which merge request !15 on system/qtcurve holds. The fork
wyn/qtcurve holds work/firefox-theme. Merge request !29 on system/qtcurve
holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

